rownowaznik: "<p>The Wilanów dial gives three readings from a single shadow: equal hours, Italian hours counted from the last sunset, and Babylonian hours counted from sunrise. True solar time at Wilanów never agrees with a mechanical clock — the gap runs between roughly ten and forty minutes across the year. The instrument lets you set a date and a clock reading, then read the shadow off three separate grids of lines.</p>"
