<p>A stucco sundial went up on the garden front of Wilanów Palace, on the south-eastern corner pavilion, around 1684. Not one dial but three: equal hours in the centre, Italian hours on the left counted from the last sunset, Babylonian hours on the right counted from sunrise. One sun, one rod, one shadow — and three different hours, depending on which grid that shadow falls on.</p>

<p class="note">A photograph of the surviving dial and a description of its medallion: {% zrodlo "widacka-2008", "a museum article by Hanna Widacka" %} (in Polish). The only scholarly study we know of devoted to Kochański's work at Wilanów: {% zrodlo "fijalkowski-1989", "Wojciech Fijałkowski, Studia Wilanowskie XI (1989)" %} — the museum offers a scan, but without a text layer, so we have not read it yet.</p>

